{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 807 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "29dfbe274e43b5bb82d30bdd9e96b12b7841282400e6ea6924a329c6c0515a5e" :edb/db-before-t 806 :edb/db-after-t 807 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534119 50 #inst "2026-10-06T03:24:25.032Z" 13194139534119 true] [17592186087779 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277783 13194139534119 true] [17592186087779 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277794 13194139534119 true] [17592186087780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277776 13194139534119 true] [17592186087780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277787 13194139534119 true] [17592186088064 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534119 true] [17592186088064 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/b12eb6672d263655f9f77eaafbf486a7be5bf9b7673c73fd0d75382d192a658b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186088064 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/q-279153.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above? {{field-1}} $= 1$" 13194139534119 false] [17592186088064 1145 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277777 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1089 "q-115135" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1100 "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1113 #uuid "26228f75-ba8b-5cfd-bc2f-68ab172288f0" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277776 1145 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=100$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=100,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{100}=10.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=10,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 10=20,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277778 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277779 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277780 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277781 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277782 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1041 "selection" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277778 13194139534119 true] [17592186277777 1110 #uuid "24cb62ba-b7a1-56fb-bbb4-e161804e0324" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277778 1034 "$20$ and $10$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534119 true] [17592186277778 1111 #uuid "98d34774-ec2d-59a3-a2cc-a70ee850eb03" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277779 1034 "$5$ and $2.5$" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534119 true] [17592186277779 1111 #uuid "0f3ab75e-f101-5f93-9447-26bba28956e3" 13194139534119 true] [17592186277780 1034 "$100$ and $25$" 1